    "raw": "\\*Entropy at 298 K estimated. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-1800 K: $Cp^{0} = 15.469 + 4.602 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.204 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ $H^{0} - H_{298}^{0} = 15.469 \\times 10^{-3} T + 2.301 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 0.204 \\times 10^{2} T^{-1} - 4.885$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1800 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -116.060 + 2.070 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 1.299 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 5.300 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ $\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = -116.060 - 2.070 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} - 1.299 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 2.650 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 61.094 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSources: Enthalpy of formation and estimated entropy at 298 K from Mills (80). Other data based on Volovik (125). ",
